ergraduate\nApply Now\nCareers in Geosciences\nPrograms\nGeology Major\nEarth and Space Sciences Major\nEarth Science Education\nGraduate\nApplicant FAQs\nGraduate Programs Handbook\nPrograms\nPhD in Geosciences\nMasters Degrees\nApply Now\nPhD. Application Fee Waivers\nResearch\nDepartment Research Areas\nDepartment Labs\nDavid E. King Field Work Award\nDEI\nOutreach\nGeology Open Nights\nGraduates for Education and Outreach (GEO)\nGiving\nTBI Field Camp\nDepartment of Geosciences\nGraduate\nApply Now\nGraduate Applications\nThank you for your interest in graduate studies in the Geosciences Department at Stony\nBrook University. For applications to the PhD in Geosciences and MS Degree with Thesis\nin Geosciences, please go to the Graduate School website.\nAPPLY NOW\nApplication Submission Deadlines:\nPhD Fall Admission - January 1\nMS Fall Admission (International Applicants) - accepted on a rolling basis through\nMay 1\nMS Fall Admission (Domestic Applicants) - accepted on a rolling basis through July\n15\nImportant Notes:\nEvaluation of MS applications will begin on January 15 and continue on a rolling basis\nuntil the indicated deadlines.\nFor applicants interested in the M.S Degree with a concentration in Hydrogeology,\nplease contact the Graduate Program Director (Joel.Hurowitz@stonbrook.edu) or Academic Programs Coordinator (Rene.Andersen@stonybrook.edu) to discuss pending modifications to the program structure, currently under review\nfor implementation in the Fall 2027 semester.\n**All applications are due no later than 11:59pm on the respective deadline date**\nThere are a limited number of PhD application fee waivers available.\nAdditional requirements:\nFor the M.A.T. Earth Sciences program, or if you wish to take any course as a non-matriculated\nstudent, the requirements may differ, and you must apply to the School of Professional Development.\nFor admission to the Graduate Program in Geosciences, the following are required,\nin addition to the Graduate School admission requirements:\nA. Conferred Bachelor's degree in one of the earth or space sciences or in biology, chemistry, physics, mathematics,\nor engineering.\nB. A minimum average of B for all undergraduate coursework and a B average for courses\nin the sciences.\nC. Acceptance by both the Department and the Graduate School\nIn special cases, a student not meeting requirements A and B may be admitted on a\nprovisional basis. Upon admission, the student will be informed of the requirements\nthat must be satisfied for termination of provisional status.\nPLEASE NOTE: Graduate Record Examination (GRE) General Test scores will not be considered\nor accepted in application materials.\n*This applies to all programs except for the M.A.T. Earth Sciences Program. For\nM.A.T. admission requirements, please visit the School of Professional Development.\nFor more information on applications, please contact:\nRene Andersen, Academic Programs Coordinator\nEmail: Rene.Andersen@stonybrook.edu\nPhone: 1-631-632-8554\nFor further information on the Geosciences MS and PhD programs, please contact:\nProfessor Joel Hurowitz, Graduate Program Director\nEmail: Joel.Hurowitz@stonybrook.edu\nPhone: 1-631-632-5355\nFor further information on the Masters in Teaching (M.A.T.) Earth and Space Science,\nplease contact:\nProfessor Gregory Henkes\nEmail: Gregory.Henkes@stonybrook.edu\nPhone: 1-631-632-2905\nFooter\nDepartment of Geosciences\n255 Earth and Space Science Building | Stony Brook, NY 11794-2100\nPHONE: (631) 632-8200\nPrivacy Policy\nReporting Discrimination\nSexual Misconduct\nAccessibility Barrier\n\u00a9 2026 Stony Brook University\n\u00a9", "links": [["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/"], ["Department of Geosciences", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/geosciences/index.html"], ["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/geosciences/index.html"], ["About", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/geosciences/about/"], ["Contact Us", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/geosciences/about/contact-us.html"], ["Depart